IMPORT prelude

-- Duties Act 2008 (Western Australia) -- vehicle licence duty (Chapter 5: ss 229, 230, 236, 238).
--
-- Edition: compilation of the Duties Act 2008 (Act No. 11 of 2008) as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49812.txt (legislation.wa.gov.au mrdoc 49812, retrieved 2026-09-07). The deposit states no
-- compilation number or date; the last entry in its compilation table is the Help to Buy (Commonwealth Powers) Act 2025 Pt. 4
-- Div. 1 (in operation 19 Dec 2025). THE FORMULA FOR R IN s 236(2)(b) IS MISSING FROM THE .txt DEPOSIT: only "(rounded to 2
-- decimal places); where -- DV is the dutiable value" survives. R is therefore an INPUT here.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. au/wa:REQ-0004 (subjects/au/wa/requirements.jsonl), priority 1, raised 9 times by the three Western Australian
-- cradle-to-grave lives. This module answers Chloe c074 (2034-06-15): "What duty on a $28,000 car". The transfer duty
-- questions are in da-property.l4.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the dutiable value rules (s 237 manufacturer's list price for prescribed new vehicles, s 238 open-market value,
-- s 239 specialised vehicles -- the value is an input); who is liable (s 232); exemptions and nominal duty (ss 240-250); the
-- "heavy vehicle" definition, which s 228 borrows from the Road Traffic (Vehicles) Act 2012 (an input flag).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Duties Act 2008 -- vehicle licence duty`

§§ `s 236 -- amount of duty`

-- s 229: "Duty is imposed on the grant or transfer of a licence for a vehicle."
-- s 236(1): the amount is worked out under this section "(rounded down to the nearest 5 cents)".
-- s 236(2), not a heavy vehicle: "(a) if the dutiable value of the vehicle does not exceed $25 000 -- 2.75% of the dutiable
-- value; or (b) if the dutiable value of the vehicle exceeds $25 000 but does not exceed $50 000 -- R% of the dutiable value,
-- where R is determined in accordance with the following formula -- [formula absent from the deposit] (rounded to 2 decimal
-- places); where -- DV is the dutiable value; or (c) if the dutiable value of the vehicle exceeds $50 000 -- 6.5% of the
-- dutiable value."
-- s 236(3), a heavy vehicle: "the lesser of -- (a) 3% of the dutiable value; and (b) $12 000."
-- s 238(1): for a vehicle not under s 237 (e.g. a used car), the dutiable value is "the amount for which the vehicle might
-- reasonably be sold, free of encumbrances, in the open market".

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `the dutiable value` IS A NUMBER, `is a heavy vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN, `R` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the vehicle licence duty before rounding` MEANS
    IF `is a heavy vehicle`
    THEN `the lesser of` (`the dutiable value` TIMES 3 DIVIDED BY 100) 12000
    ELSE IF `the dutiable value` AT MOST 25000
         THEN `the dutiable value` TIMES 2.75 DIVIDED BY 100
         ELSE IF `the dutiable value` AT MOST 50000
              THEN `the dutiable value` TIMES `R` DIVIDED BY 100
              ELSE `the dutiable value` TIMES 6.5 DIVIDED BY 100

-- `R` is the percentage under s 236(2)(b), already rounded to 2 decimal places; it is used only when the dutiable value
-- exceeds $25 000 but not $50 000 and the vehicle is not heavy.
GIVEN `the dutiable value` IS A NUMBER, `is a heavy vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN, `R` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the vehicle licence duty` MEANS
    FLOOR (`the vehicle licence duty before rounding` `the dutiable value` `is a heavy vehicle` `R` TIMES 20) DIVIDED BY 20
